Article 8

Assistants have the duties to:
a. provide sufficient information to victims about their rights; b. provide psychosocial services to victims so that victims feel safe and comfortable;
c. assist victims during the examination and medical recovery process; d. assist victims during the medicolegal process;
e. assist victims during the examination process at the police, prosecutor's office and court;
f. assist victims while in the safe house;
g. monitor the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the police, prosecutor's office and court;
h. maintain the privacy and confidentiality of victims' identities from all parties who have no interest, including reporting by mass media; i. coordinate with other assistants; and j. provide continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

